bridge-ielts-06-academic-listening-test-3-4.mp3","question_groups":[{"id":"en-c6-t3-l-g4-0","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"matching_features","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 31-34","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><p>Choose the correct letter, A, B or C.</p></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">31</strong> According to the speaker, it is not clear</span><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c6-t3-l-q31\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>when the farming economy was introduced to Ireland.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c6-t3-l-q31\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>why people began to farm in Ireland.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c6-t3-l-q31\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>where the early Irish farmers came from.</span></div></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">32</strong> What point does the speaker make about breeding animals in Neolithic Ireland?</span><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c6-t3-l-q32\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>Their numbers must have been above a certain level.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c6-t3-l-q32\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>They were under threat from wild animals.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c6-t3-l-q32\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>Some species died out during this period.</span></div></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">33</strong> What does the speaker say about the transportation of animals?</span><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c6-t3-l-q33\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>Livestock would have limited the distance the farmers could sail.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c6-t3-l-q33\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>Neolithic boats were too primitive to have been used.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c6-t3-l-q33\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>Probably only a few breeding animals were imported.</span></div></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">34</strong> What is the main evidence for cereal crops in Neolithic Ireland?</span><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c6-t3-l-q34\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>the remains of burnt grain in pots</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c6-t3-l-q34\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>the marks left on pots by grains</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c6-t3-l-q34\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>the patterns painted on the surface of pots</span></div></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":4},{"id":"en-c6-t3-l-g4-1","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 35-40","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><div class=\"source-section-content-wrapper\"><p>Complete the sentences below.</p><p>Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS for each answer.</p><p><strong>STONE TOOLS</strong></p><ul><li>Ploughs could either have been pulled by <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">35</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c6-t3-l-q35\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> or by cattle.</li><li>The farmers needed homes which were permanent dwellings.</li><li>In the final stages of axe-making, water and <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">36</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c6-t3-l-q36\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> were necessary for grinding and polishing.</li><li>Irish axes were exported from Ireland to <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">37</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c6-t3-l-q37\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> and England.</li></ul><p><strong>POTTERY MAKING</strong></p><ul><li>The colonisers used clay to make pots.</li><li>The <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">38</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c6-t3-l-q38\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> of the pots was often polished to make them watertight.</li><li>Clay from <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">39</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c6-t3-l-q39\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> areas was generally used.</li><li>Decoration was only put around the <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">40</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c6-t3-l-q40\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> of the earliest pots.</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":6}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/cambridge-ielts-06-academic-listening-test-3-4.mp3"],"order_index":4}],"questions":[{"id":"en-c6-t3-l-q1","part_id":"en-c6-t3-l-p1","group_id":"en-c6-t3-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"Select","correct_answer_variants":["Select"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[1],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_3166480_1","order_index":1,"points":1},{"id":"en-c6-t3-l-q2","part_id":"en-c6-t3-l-p1","group_id":"en-c6-t3-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"1973","correct_answer_variants":["1973"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[2],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_3166480_2","order_index":2,"points":1},{"id":"en-c6-t3-l-q3","part_id":"en-c6-t3-l-p1","group_id":"en-c6-t3-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"15 Riverside","correct_answer_variants":["15 Riverside"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[3],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_3166480_3","order_index":3,"points":1},{"id":"en-c6-t3-l-q4","part_id":"en-c6-t3-l-p1","group_id":"en-c6-t3-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"2 weeks","correct_answer_variants":["2 weeks"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[4],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_3166480_4","order_index":4,"points":1},{"id":"en-c6-t3-l-q5","part_id":"en-c6-t3-l-p1","group_id":"en-c6-t3-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"616295","correct_answer_variants":["616295"],"answerCount":1,"s